/T (Instruction format n-operand format To reduce instruction size and thereby reduce program storage space it is common to specify only m<n operands explicitly in the instruction, remaining operands are implicit Explicit address fields usually refer to main memory implicit ones refer to registers If m is the maximum number of explicit main memory addresses allowed in any processor instruction, the processor may be called an m-address machine Implicit input operands must be placed in locations known to the processor before the instruction that refers to them is executed)
/E (Instruction format n-operand format To reduce instruction size and thereby reduce program storage space it is common to specify only m<n operands explicitly in the instruction, remaining operands are implicit Explicit address fields usually refer to main memory implicit ones refer to registers If m is the maximum number of explicit main memory addresses allowed in any processor instruction, the processor may be called an m-address machine Implicit input operands must be placed in locations known to the processor before the instruction that refers to them is executed)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
