/T (Immediate addressing:  X  \(Operand\) is constant, its value can be placed in the instruction operand field Direct addressing: X \(Operand\) is variable, then operand field X contains address of the memory location of  the operand. Requires one fetch operation for getting the operand. Indirect addressing: Instruction operand  field contains the address W of a storage location which in turn contains address X of the desired operand. By changing the content of W, address of the operand value required by the instruction is effectively changed Requires two fetch operation for getting the operand.)
/E (Immediate addressing:  X  \(Operand\) is constant, its value can be placed in the instruction operand field Direct addressing: X \(Operand\) is variable, then operand field X contains address of the memory location of  the operand. Requires one fetch operation for getting the operand. Indirect addressing: Instruction operand  field contains the address W of a storage location which in turn contains address X of the desired operand. By changing the content of W, address of the operand value required by the instruction is effectively changed Requires two fetch operation for getting the operand.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0 1 2]
>>
