/T (Absolute addressing: Direct addressing needs the complete operand address Partial addressing information is included in the instruction, so the complete \(absolute\) operand address must be constructed by the processor Relative addressing: Operand field contains a relative address or displacement D Absolute or effective address \(A\) = Single address register from a set of general purpose registers associated with the operand \(R\) + Displacement \(D\))
/E (Absolute addressing: Direct addressing needs the complete operand address Partial addressing information is included in the instruction, so the complete \(absolute\) operand address must be constructed by the processor Relative addressing: Operand field contains a relative address or displacement D Absolute or effective address \(A\) = Single address register from a set of general purpose registers associated with the operand \(R\) + Displacement \(D\))
/Pg 9 0 R
