/T (Reduced instruction set computer \(RISC\) Developed at IBM in the mid 1970s Relatively few instruction types and addressing modes Fixed and easily decoded instruction format Fast single cycle instruction execution Hardware rather than micro program control   Memory access limited mainly to load and store instructions Use of compilers to optimize object code performance Most RISC instructions involve only register-to-register operations that are internal to the CPU     Reduces execution time to single cycle     Allows CPU cycle time and hardware complexity to be minimized Complex instructions are implemented by routines due to the unavailability of the complex instructions in the instruction set)
/E (Reduced instruction set computer \(RISC\) Developed at IBM in the mid 1970s Relatively few instruction types and addressing modes Fixed and easily decoded instruction format Fast single cycle instruction execution Hardware rather than micro program control   Memory access limited mainly to load and store instructions Use of compilers to optimize object code performance Most RISC instructions involve only register-to-register operations that are internal to the CPU     Reduces execution time to single cycle     Allows CPU cycle time and hardware complexity to be minimized Complex instructions are implemented by routines due to the unavailability of the complex instructions in the instruction set)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
